module proxSeqDetection
module viabilityDetection
module plaDetection
module seqLibraryQC

manifest JurkatCells
manifest RajiCells
manifest PBS
manifest ProxSeqProbeA
manifest ProxSeqProbeB
manifest FreeOligoA
manifest FreeOligoB
manifest LigationBuffer
manifest Ligase
manifest BlockingBuffer
manifest WashBuffer
manifest DNALibraryBuffer
manifest SequencingReagent
manifest IsotypeControlAntibody
manifest StopSolution

// ============================================================
// Computational Prediction of Protein Interactions in Single
// Cells by Proximity Sequencing.
// Xia J, Phan HV, Vistain L, Chen M, Khan AA, Tay S (2024)
// PLoS Comput Biol 20(3): e1011915.
// DOI: 10.1371/journal.pcbi.1011915
//
// This BioScript file encodes the experimental Prox-seq
// (Proximity Sequencing) protocol as described in the paper.
// Prox-seq simultaneously measures gene expression, protein
// expression, and protein complexes on single cells using a
// proximity ligation assay (PLA) with DNA-conjugated antibody
// probes (Probe A and Probe B). Ligation occurs only when
// two protein molecules are within 50-70 nm of each other.
// PLA products are sequenced alongside scRNA-seq cDNA
// libraries to yield multi-omic single-cell data.
//
// TWO CELL LINE ARMS encoded in sequence:
//   ARM 1: Jurkat T cells (CD3, CD28, PD1, CD147, ICAM1,
//           PDL1, HLADR, B7 protein panel)
//   ARM 2: Raji B cells (same probe panel, different
//           protein complex landscape)
//
// FREE OLIGO MODIFICATION: An experimentally modified
// Prox-seq procedure measures non-proximal (unligated)
// probes via FreeOligoA and FreeOligoB. These non-proximal
// counts are used by the linear regression (LR) method and
// ensemble method for proximity noise estimation.
//
// ISOTYPE CONTROL: IsotypeControlAntibody with
// oligonucleotide conjugation is included in both probe
// panels to estimate nonspecific antibody binding
// probability directly from observed data (Section 2.2).
//
// CFG STRUCTURE:
//   BB1  main              -- entry: cell prep, Prox-seq
//                             probe staining, ligation, and
//                             library prep for Jurkat arm
//   BB2  jurkatLibPass     -- jurkatLibSignal > 0: library
//                             QC passed; dispose and proceed
//   BB3  jurkatLibFail     -- jurkatLibSignal <= 0: library
//                             failed; drain Jurkat products
//   BB4  jurkatLibJoin     -- join: Raji B cell arm begins
//   BB5  rajiLibPass       -- rajiLibSignal > 0: library
//                             QC passed; dispose Raji products
//   BB6  rajiLibFail       -- rajiLibSignal <= 0: library
//                             failed; drain Raji products
//   BB7  finalCleanup      -- terminal: dispose QC signals;
//                             experiment ends; data sent for
//                             computational analysis
//
// NOTE ON LIGATION DISTANCE: The BioScript ligation step
// is abstracted via `mix`. Physical ligation occurs in the
// 50-70 nm proximity window defined by the DNA oligo linker
// length. Only Probe A + Probe B pairs within this distance
// produce a PLA product (dual-barcode requirement enforced
// at sequencing alignment stage, not modelled here).
//
// NOTE ON UMI COUNTING: PLA product quantification by
// counting unique molecular identifiers (UMIs) is performed
// computationally (off-chip, Python3/Anaconda3 v4.10.3).
// Code: https://github.com/tay-lab/Prox-seq_computation
// Raw data: GEO accession GSE196130.
//
// NOTE ON DURATION TOKENS: BioScript supports `s` (seconds)
// and `m` (minutes) only. All incubation times are
// expressed accordingly.
// ============================================================

instructions:

// ============================================================
// BB1: main
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 1 - STEP 1: Prepare Jurkat T cell suspension.
//   Jurkat cells cultured under standard conditions.
//   Resuspend in PBS at appropriate concentration for
//   single-cell staining with Prox-seq probe panel.
//   Isotype control antibody included in probe panel
//   to estimate nonspecific binding background (Section 2.2).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

jurkatCells       = dispense 1 units of JurkatCells
cellPBS           = dispense 1 units of PBS
jurkatSuspension  = mix jurkatCells with cellPBS for 5m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 1 - STEP 2: Block nonspecific binding sites.
//   Incubate cells with blocking buffer for 10 min at 4 C
//   prior to Prox-seq probe addition. This reduces background
//   from nonspecific antibody binding (Section 2.2).
//   Paper notes nonspecific binding constitutes <1% of
//   both-specific PLA counts for extracellular proteins
//   (e.g. CD147:CD147 in Jurkat cells, S4 Fig).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

blockingBuf       = dispense 1 units of BlockingBuffer
blockedCells      = mix jurkatSuspension with blockingBuf for 10m
heat blockedCells at 4c for 10m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 1 - STEP 3: Stain with Prox-seq Probe A panel.
//   Each target protein is stained with a DNA-conjugated
//   Probe A antibody. Panel targets: CD3, CD28, PD1, CD147,
//   ICAM1, PDL1, HLADR, B7 (same panel as Ref [4]).
//   Isotype control antibody (oligonucleotide-conjugated)
//   included in Probe A panel for nonspecific binding QC.
//   Incubate 30 min at 4 C.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

probeAStain       = dispense 1 units of ProxSeqProbeA
isotypeControl    = dispense 1 units of IsotypeControlAntibody
probeAWithControl = mix probeAStain with isotypeControl for 5s
probeAStained     = mix blockedCells with probeAWithControl for 30m
heat probeAStained at 4c for 30m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 1 - STEP 4: Wash to remove unbound Probe A.
//   Wash cells 3x with PBS to remove excess unbound
//   Probe A antibodies. Unbound probes do not contribute
//   to PLA signal because library preparation and sequence
//   alignment require barcodes from both Probe A and B.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

wash1A = dispense 1 units of WashBuffer
wash2A = dispense 1 units of WashBuffer
wash3A = dispense 1 units of WashBuffer

washedA1 = mix probeAStained with wash1A for 2m
washedA2 = mix washedA1 with wash2A for 2m
jurkatProbeAReady = mix washedA2 with wash3A for 2m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 1 - STEP 5: Stain with Prox-seq Probe B panel.
//   Each target protein is stained with a DNA-conjugated
//   Probe B antibody (same protein targets as Probe A panel).
//   Isotype control antibody (oligonucleotide-conjugated)
//   included in Probe B panel as well.
//   Incubate 30 min at 4 C.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

probeBStain       = dispense 1 units of ProxSeqProbeB
probeBStained     = mix jurkatProbeAReady with probeBStain for 30m
heat probeBStained at 4c for 30m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 1 - STEP 6: Wash to remove unbound Probe B.
//   Wash 3x with PBS. After washing, cells carry both
//   Probe A and Probe B antibodies on surface proteins.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

wash1B = dispense 1 units of WashBuffer
wash2B = dispense 1 units of WashBuffer
wash3B = dispense 1 units of WashBuffer

washedB1 = mix probeBStained with wash1B for 2m
washedB2 = mix washedB1 with wash2B for 2m
jurkatDualStained = mix washedB2 with wash3B for 2m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 1 - STEP 7: Add Free Oligo probes (non-proximal
//   probe measurement modification).
//   FreeOligoA and FreeOligoB are added to measure the
//   non-proximal (unligated) probe counts. Free oligos
//   are not conjugated to antibodies; they generate
//   PLA products of the form:
//     Protein_X : free_oligo_B  (counts non-proximal Probe A)
//     free_oligo_A : Protein_Y  (counts non-proximal Probe B)
//   These non-proximal counts are essential for the LR
//   method and ensemble method (Section: LR method, Eq. 5).
//   Reference: Vistain et al. Nat Methods 2022 [4].
// ------------------------------------------------------------

freeOligoADrop = dispense 1 units of FreeOligoA
freeOligoBDrop = dispense 1 units of FreeOligoB

freeOligoMix = mix freeOligoADrop with freeOligoBDrop for 5s
jurkatWithFreeOligos = mix jurkatDualStained with freeOligoMix for 10m
heat jurkatWithFreeOligos at 4c for 10m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 1 - STEP 8: Proximity ligation reaction.
//   Add ligation buffer and T4 DNA ligase. Ligation occurs
//   between Probe A oligo and Probe B oligo only when the
//   two probes are within 50-70 nm of each other (i.e.,
//   their target proteins are co-localised or in complex).
//   Ligation distance threshold = 50 nm in simulation model.
//   Incubate at room temperature (25 C) for 30 min.
//   NOTE: `mix` abstracts the proximity ligation event.
//   PLA products (ligated A+B barcodes) are the signal.
//   Random co-localisation generates proximity noise:
//   E(X_ij) = (d_ligation^2 / 4R^2) * A_i * B_j
//   (Methods: Theoretical calculation of proximity noise).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

ligBuf            = dispense 1 units of LigationBuffer
ligase            = dispense 1 units of Ligase
ligationReagents  = mix ligBuf with ligase for 5s
jurkatLigated     = mix jurkatWithFreeOligos with ligationReagents for 30m
heat jurkatLigated at 25c for 30m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 1 - STEP 9: Stop ligation and wash.
//   Add stop solution to quench ligase activity.
//   Wash 3x with PBS to remove ligation reagents prior
//   to single-cell encapsulation / library preparation.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

stopSol       = dispense 1 units of StopSolution
jurkatStopped = mix jurkatLigated with stopSol for 5m

wash1L = dispense 1 units of WashBuffer
wash2L = dispense 1 units of WashBuffer
wash3L = dispense 1 units of WashBuffer

washedL1 = mix jurkatStopped with wash1L for 2m
washedL2 = mix washedL1 with wash2L for 2m
jurkatLigatedReady = mix washedL2 with wash3L for 2m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 1 - STEP 10: Single-cell encapsulation and
//   library preparation (scRNA-seq + Prox-seq).
//   Cells are encapsulated in individual droplets (10x
//   Genomics or equivalent microfluidic platform) and
//   lysed. mRNA is captured by poly-dT oligonucleotides.
//   PLA products are captured by their barcoded sequences.
//   cDNA (gene expression) and PLA product libraries are
//   generated simultaneously and sequenced together.
//   DNA library buffer is added to prepare the combined
//   library for sequencing.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

dnaLibBuf        = dispense 1 units of DNALibraryBuffer
jurkatLibPrep    = mix jurkatLigatedReady with dnaLibBuf for 30m
heat jurkatLibPrep at 37c for 30m

seqReagentJ      = dispense 1 units of SequencingReagent
jurkatSeqReady   = mix jurkatLibPrep with seqReagentJ for 10m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 1 - STEP 11: Library QC detection.
//   QC check on the Jurkat Prox-seq library before
//   sequencing. Checks for adequate library complexity,
//   correct fragment sizes for PLA products and cDNA,
//   and sufficient UMI diversity.
//   proxSeqDetection module abstracts fluorometric/
//   electrophoretic QC (e.g. Bioanalyzer, Qubit).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

jurkatLibSignal = detect seqLibraryQC on jurkatSeqReady for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB2 / BB3: Jurkat library QC gate
// Pass (BB2): jurkatLibSignal > 0 -> library QC passed;
//             dispose Jurkat library products and proceed
//             to Raji B cell arm.
// Fail (BB3): jurkatLibSignal <= 0 -> library prep failed
//             (low complexity, wrong fragment sizes, or
//             insufficient UMIs); drain Jurkat products.
// Both branches converge at BB4 (jurkatLibJoin).
// ============================================================

if (jurkatLibSignal > 0) {
    dispose jurkatSeqReady
} else {
    drain jurkatSeqReady
}

// ============================================================
// BB4: jurkatLibJoin
// Dispose Jurkat library QC signal. Control falls into
// Raji B cell arm (BB5/BB6).
// ============================================================

dispose jurkatLibSignal

// ============================================================
// ARM 2: Raji B Cell Prox-seq Protocol
// Identical probe panel and procedural steps as Jurkat arm.
// Raji cells express ICAM1 (known homodimer on cell surface,
// Ref [14]), HLADR, PDL1 among other panel proteins.
// The ensemble method recovers ICAM1:ICAM1 complex
// in Raji cells (Fig 5d-f, paper Section: Comparison of
// all three analytical methods to real data).
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 2 - STEP 1: Prepare Raji B cell suspension.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

rajiCells        = dispense 1 units of RajiCells
cellPBS2         = dispense 1 units of PBS
rajiSuspension   = mix rajiCells with cellPBS2 for 5m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 2 - STEP 2: Block nonspecific binding sites.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

blockingBuf2     = dispense 1 units of BlockingBuffer
rajiBlocked      = mix rajiSuspension with blockingBuf2 for 10m
heat rajiBlocked at 4c for 10m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 2 - STEP 3: Stain with Prox-seq Probe A panel.
//   Same panel as Jurkat arm (CD3, CD28, PD1, CD147,
//   ICAM1, PDL1, HLADR, B7 + isotype control).
//   Note: Raji cells do not express CD3 or PD1;
//   their PLA products for these targets are near zero,
//   validating specificity of the probe panel [4].
// ------------------------------------------------------------

probeAStain2      = dispense 1 units of ProxSeqProbeA
isotypeControl2   = dispense 1 units of IsotypeControlAntibody
probeAWithCtrl2   = mix probeAStain2 with isotypeControl2 for 5s
rajiProbeAStained = mix rajiBlocked with probeAWithCtrl2 for 30m
heat rajiProbeAStained at 4c for 30m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 2 - STEP 4: Wash to remove unbound Probe A.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

wash1A2 = dispense 1 units of WashBuffer
wash2A2 = dispense 1 units of WashBuffer
wash3A2 = dispense 1 units of WashBuffer

rajiWashedA1 = mix rajiProbeAStained with wash1A2 for 2m
rajiWashedA2 = mix rajiWashedA1 with wash2A2 for 2m
rajiProbeAReady = mix rajiWashedA2 with wash3A2 for 2m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 2 - STEP 5: Stain with Prox-seq Probe B panel.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

probeBStain2      = dispense 1 units of ProxSeqProbeB
rajiProbeBStained = mix rajiProbeAReady with probeBStain2 for 30m
heat rajiProbeBStained at 4c for 30m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 2 - STEP 6: Wash to remove unbound Probe B.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

wash1B2 = dispense 1 units of WashBuffer
wash2B2 = dispense 1 units of WashBuffer
wash3B2 = dispense 1 units of WashBuffer

rajiWashedB1 = mix rajiProbeBStained with wash1B2 for 2m
rajiWashedB2 = mix rajiWashedB1 with wash2B2 for 2m
rajiDualStained = mix rajiWashedB2 with wash3B2 for 2m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 2 - STEP 7: Add Free Oligo probes.
//   Same free oligo modification as Jurkat arm.
//   Non-proximal probe counts for Raji cells are used
//   to calibrate proximity noise in the LR and ensemble
//   methods for Raji-specific protein complex detection.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

freeOligoA2    = dispense 1 units of FreeOligoA
freeOligoB2    = dispense 1 units of FreeOligoB
freeOligoMix2  = mix freeOligoA2 with freeOligoB2 for 5s
rajiWithFreeOligos = mix rajiDualStained with freeOligoMix2 for 10m
heat rajiWithFreeOligos at 4c for 10m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 2 - STEP 8: Proximity ligation reaction.
//   Same ligation conditions as Jurkat arm.
//   Ligation distance = 50 nm threshold.
//   Proximity noise for Raji arm:
//   E(X_ij) = (d_ligation^2 / 4R^2) * A_i * B_j
//   ICAM1:ICAM1 homodimer signal exceeds expected random
//   ligation background (Fig 5d-f, paper).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

ligBuf2           = dispense 1 units of LigationBuffer
ligase2           = dispense 1 units of Ligase
ligReagents2      = mix ligBuf2 with ligase2 for 5s
rajiLigated       = mix rajiWithFreeOligos with ligReagents2 for 30m
heat rajiLigated at 25c for 30m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 2 - STEP 9: Stop ligation and wash.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

stopSol2       = dispense 1 units of StopSolution
rajiStopped    = mix rajiLigated with stopSol2 for 5m

wash1L2 = dispense 1 units of WashBuffer
wash2L2 = dispense 1 units of WashBuffer
wash3L2 = dispense 1 units of WashBuffer

rajiWashedL1 = mix rajiStopped with wash1L2 for 2m
rajiWashedL2 = mix rajiWashedL1 with wash2L2 for 2m
rajiLigatedReady = mix rajiWashedL2 with wash3L2 for 2m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 2 - STEP 10: Single-cell encapsulation and
//   library preparation.
//   Same procedure as Jurkat arm.
//   Combined cDNA + PLA product library generated.
//   After sequencing, UMI counts per PLA product per
//   single Raji cell are the primary data for downstream
//   computational analysis (iterative, LR, ensemble methods).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

dnaLibBuf2       = dispense 1 units of DNALibraryBuffer
rajiLibPrep      = mix rajiLigatedReady with dnaLibBuf2 for 30m
heat rajiLibPrep at 37c for 30m

seqReagentR      = dispense 1 units of SequencingReagent
rajiSeqReady     = mix rajiLibPrep with seqReagentR for 10m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 2 - STEP 11: Library QC detection.
//   Same QC procedure as Jurkat arm.
//   seqLibraryQC module abstracts Bioanalyzer/Qubit QC.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

rajiLibSignal = detect seqLibraryQC on rajiSeqReady for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB5 / BB6: Raji library QC gate
// Pass (BB5): rajiLibSignal > 0 -> library QC passed;
//             dispose all Raji library products.
// Fail (BB6): rajiLibSignal <= 0 -> library prep failed;
//             drain all Raji products.
// Both branches converge at BB7 (finalCleanup).
// ============================================================

if (rajiLibSignal > 0) {
    dispose rajiSeqReady
} else {
    drain rajiSeqReady
}

// ============================================================
// BB7: finalCleanup (terminal)
// Dispose library QC signals from both arms.
// Experiment ends. Sequencing data submitted to
// computational pipeline for proximity noise removal and
// protein complex prediction (iterative / LR / ensemble).
// Code: https://github.com/tay-lab/Prox-seq_computation
// Data: GEO GSE196130
// ============================================================

dispose rajiLibSignal

// [terminal -- no further instructions; exit node for CFG]
